# FortiGate safety

## Read-only default

When FortiGate craft is authorized, these are fine without a mutate verb:

| Surface | Tools |
| --- | --- |
| Devices / health | `list_devices`, `get_device_status`, `test_device_connection`, `health`, `test_connection`, `discover_vdoms`, `get_schema_info` |
| Interfaces | `list_interfaces`, `get_interface_status` |
| Policies (read) | `list_firewall_policies`, `get_firewall_policy_detail` |
| Objects (read) | `list_address_objects`, `list_service_objects`, `list_virtual_ips`, `get_virtual_ip_detail` |
| Routes (read) | `get_routing_table`, `list_static_routes`, `get_static_route_detail` |

Do **not** call any of the following unless the user gave an explicit verb
this turn naming the target (device_id, policy_id, object/VIP name,
route_id, or clear create intent):

| Mutate | Tools |
| --- | --- |
| Register / remove MCP device | `add_device`, `remove_device` |
| Policy create / update / delete | `create_firewall_policy`, `update_firewall_policy`, `delete_firewall_policy` |
| Address / service create | `create_address_object`, `create_service_object` |
| VIP create / update / delete | `create_virtual_ip`, `update_virtual_ip`, `delete_virtual_ip` |
| Static route create / update / delete | `create_static_route`, `update_static_route`, `delete_static_route` |

Bare product name ("FortiGate") alone is **not** mutate authorization.

## Irreversible — confirm blast radius

Before proceeding when clearly authorized:

| Action | State risk |
| --- | --- |
| Policy delete / broad accept | Drops or opens traffic; can cut management paths |
| Default-route change/delete | Can blackhole the firewall or all downstream nets |
| VIP delete / remap | Breaks DNAT / published services |
| `remove_device` | Drops the device from this MCP registry (not the appliance OS) |
| `add_device` with credentials | Handles secrets — never echo password/api_token in chat |

State the object (id/name) and consequence in one sentence, then act only
if authorization already covers that loss.

## Credential posture

- Prefer API-token auth fields over pasting long-lived passwords into
  tool args when the user offers a choice.
- Never reprint `password` or `api_token` values from `add_device` args or
  tool output into the chat receipt.
- If a secret appeared in tool output by mistake, say so and recommend
  rotation — do not repeat the value.

## Defaults

1. Prefer the smallest mutate that satisfies the ask (update one policy
   field set over recreate; single key object over bulk).
2. Prefer listing/detail before every mutate so receipts name real ids.
3. Prefer reusing listed address/service objects over creating duplicates.
4. Refuse "open everything" / any-any accept without a named src, dst,
   service, and interfaces.
5. Prefer MCP tools discovered on the live FortiGate MCP
   (`user-mcp_fortigate`); do not invent tool names.
6. Neighbor firewall / cloud NGFW products are out of scope.

